      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PART A: BASIC CONCEPT OF CLIMATE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Weather refers to short-term atmospheric conditions, while climate represents long-term patterns over extended periods.",
        "Key factors influencing regional climate include latitude, altitude, distance from the sea (continentality), ocean currents, relief features, and prevailing winds.",
        "Köppen's scheme divides global climates into five primary groups designated by letters A, B, C, D, and E.",
        "Climatic conditions directly determine the type and density of natural vegetation present in any geographic region."
      ],
      "id": "gwynn2a"
    },
